1
00:03:48,436 --> 00:03:49,646
Look behind you!

2
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:58,071
<i>That's it!</i>

3
00:03:58,154 --> 00:04:00,031
You're really getting
carried away, Bulots.

4
00:04:00,114 --> 00:04:03,243
What's going on
between you and Kenzo in your fanfic?

5
00:04:05,912 --> 00:04:07,747
You were kidnapped by gang members,

6
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:09,958
and then he rescued you.

7
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:11,417
But the thing is,

8
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:12,835
he got shot.

9
00:04:15,421 --> 00:04:17,048
Janine, run now!

10
00:04:17,131 --> 00:04:19,926
Instead, you ran straight to him.

11
00:04:20,009 --> 00:04:21,803
Kenzo! Kenzo, my love!

12
00:04:21,886 --> 00:04:23,680
Are you okay, my love?

13
00:04:24,472 --> 00:04:27,141
Kenzo! Oh my god!

14
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:32,522
You really like making a scene, huh?

15
00:04:32,605 --> 00:04:34,357
You're thinking too far ahead.

16
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,567
I'm just on Chapter 14.

17
00:04:38,152 --> 00:04:40,363
You're already spoiling my ending, huh?

18
00:04:40,446 --> 00:04:44,033
The only ending I know is
Attorney Mendes glaring at you

19
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:46,327
because you're more focused on your fanfic

20
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:47,787
than on studying.

21
00:04:48,454 --> 00:04:49,998
Really?

22
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:52,083
How do I stay awake?

23
00:04:52,834 --> 00:04:53,793
Like this.

24
00:04:53,876 --> 00:04:54,961
Like this?

25
00:04:55,628 --> 00:04:56,504
Huh?

26
00:04:57,338 --> 00:04:58,214
Like this?

27
00:05:03,219 --> 00:05:04,429
Your breath smells bad.

28
00:05:07,724 --> 00:05:09,809
Why did you buy so much chewing gum?

29
00:05:09,892 --> 00:05:13,146
There are lucky Mint 2 Be wrappers
containing tickets

30
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:15,273
to an intimate fan meet

31
00:05:15,356 --> 00:05:17,775
with my dear Kenzo.

32
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:19,193
I need to win one.

33
00:05:19,277 --> 00:05:20,820
You're being delusional again.

34
00:05:22,238 --> 00:05:23,364
Why do you care?

35
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:26,409
As long as it's for my Kenzo,

36
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:27,368
yes.

37
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:33,750
There you go.

38
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:35,668
Just sleep it off.

39
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:38,046
After all, you and Kenzo
only see each other in your dreams.

40
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:39,380
Whoa.

41
00:05:39,922 --> 00:05:41,424
You're a hater now?

42
00:05:42,759 --> 00:05:44,385
Hey! My phone!

43
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:45,553
It's yours.

44
00:05:45,636 --> 00:05:47,472
Thanks.

45
00:05:58,608 --> 00:05:59,484
How's the story for you, Pip?

46
00:05:59,567 --> 00:06:01,736
EVEN AS THE RAIN POURS HEAVILY,
I CAN STILL HEAR MY HEART BEATING.

47
00:06:01,819 --> 00:06:02,904
I WORRY ABOUT YOU.

48
00:06:02,987 --> 00:06:03,821
It's fine.

49
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:05,615
But why does it always have to be raining?

50
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:07,575
Duh!

51
00:06:07,658 --> 00:06:09,243
It's more romantic that way!

52
00:06:09,327 --> 00:06:12,038
There's got to be
those rainy effects there!

53
00:06:13,164 --> 00:06:16,876
It's not very romantic when you end
up with a cold and a fever, right?

54
00:06:16,959 --> 00:06:18,920
You know what? You talk too much.

55
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:20,088
I'm ignoring you,

56
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:21,547
your bad looks,

57
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:23,299
and your bad breath!

58
00:06:23,382 --> 00:06:24,926
I'm also ignoring those without abs,

59
00:06:25,009 --> 00:06:26,385
the single since birth!

60
00:06:27,011 --> 00:06:28,304
And last of all…

61
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,264
I'm ignoring the haters.

62
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:33,184
I'm going to sleep.
You'd better turn the lights out.

63
00:06:38,022 --> 00:06:39,816
Just go for it, you losers!

64
00:06:40,691 --> 00:06:43,277
Gosh! You're unbelievable!

65
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:46,155
Just do it already!

66
00:06:48,866 --> 00:06:51,494
- Hey, you're here.
- You're loud. Know what time it is?

67
00:06:51,577 --> 00:06:52,537
Let me guess.

68
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:54,288
You just came from Janine's, didn't you?

69
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:57,750
Oh great. It's like I don't even have
a roommate anymore!

70
00:06:57,834 --> 00:06:58,751
Of course I was…

71
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,670
Wait!

72
00:07:01,587 --> 00:07:02,630
Otep.

73
00:07:03,881 --> 00:07:05,383
Damn it!

74
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:08,803
Sorry.

75
00:07:09,345 --> 00:07:10,513
What were you saying?

76
00:07:10,596 --> 00:07:12,765
As I said, I promised Aunt Marissa

77
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:15,309
that I'd make sure Janine is safe.

78
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:16,894
Talk about strict surveillance.

79
00:07:18,604 --> 00:07:20,398
So now we keep on chewing for her,

80
00:07:20,481 --> 00:07:22,316
and all we get is "better luck next time"?

81
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:27,280
Hey!

82
00:07:27,363 --> 00:07:29,574
- Oh man! I'm telling you!
- Otep, stop it.

83
00:07:29,657 --> 00:07:31,242
I'm telling you!

84
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:32,952
You will like it.

85
00:07:33,744 --> 00:07:34,912
What is it?

86
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:36,956
Time to give up, man.

87
00:07:37,999 --> 00:07:40,001
Janine's just not into you.

88
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:43,004
One more.

89
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:45,089
There might be something in here.

90
00:07:48,968 --> 00:07:51,262
Oh!

91
00:07:51,345 --> 00:07:53,264
Wait. This is it, man. This is the one!

92
00:07:53,347 --> 00:07:54,932
- Let me see.
- Is this what it looks like?

93
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:55,850
What does it say?

94
00:07:56,559 --> 00:07:57,685
You look like a fool.

95
00:07:58,394 --> 00:07:59,270
Whatever.

96
00:08:04,942 --> 00:08:08,237
Looking at her first photo
on this dating app, it's a no.

97
00:08:08,946 --> 00:08:10,656
Love to parties?

98
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:12,366
Is this Otep?

99
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:13,701
Wrong grammar.

100
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:16,078
And this one…

101
00:08:17,413 --> 00:08:22,210
Yikes! Her biceps are bigger than yours.
She's like the Incredible Hulk.

102
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:25,963
- You'll end up getting beaten by her.
- We hope you can donate.

103
00:08:26,047 --> 00:08:28,591
- And be a lifesaver today.
- This one will beat you up.

104
00:08:28,674 --> 00:08:30,635
- Thank you.
- All right. Thank you.

105
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:35,473
I've been talking,
but you're not listening to me!

106
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:37,683
It turns out
I don't have anyone beside me.

107
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:39,310
Is this for the blood donation drive?

108
00:08:40,353 --> 00:08:43,648
Here, this one, 25 years old.

109
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:46,526
Just a bit older than you,

110
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:49,570
but this one already has
a fully developed frontal lobe.

111
00:08:51,364 --> 00:08:55,243
"Board Member, Guardians of Humanity."

112
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:57,912
"My causes and communities…"

113
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:01,374
"Volunteering and human rights…"

114
00:09:01,457 --> 00:09:03,000
So corny!

115
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:05,503
- She's too full of herself.
- Don't!

116
00:09:05,586 --> 00:09:06,712
Why?

117
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:10,258
I thought you didn't like dating apps.

118
00:09:10,341 --> 00:09:13,135
Why bother regretting it?
She's too pretentious.

119
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:15,638
She's a member of
a volunteer organization I want to join.

120
00:09:15,721 --> 00:09:17,473
And you immediately
called her pretentious?

121
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:23,604
The problem is
your profile picture is ugly.

122
00:09:24,146 --> 00:09:25,773
That's why nobody swipes right.

123
00:09:25,856 --> 00:09:27,066
I'll change it

124
00:09:27,149 --> 00:09:29,527
to one where you look
like you actually showered.

125
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:30,695
You're unbelievable.

126
00:09:34,156 --> 00:09:35,825
Not my photo gallery!

127
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:39,495
Why?

128
00:09:40,538 --> 00:09:42,290
Are you hiding something from me?

129
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:45,334
- What?
- A scandal.

130
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:46,502
Hey!

131
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:49,338
Hey! I already saw that.

132
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:51,924
- Come on--
- I've already seen that.

133
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:53,342
I've already seen that.

134
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:54,885
- Don't be loud.
- Ouch!

135
00:09:54,969 --> 00:09:57,096
Why? Do you have a scandal?

136
00:09:59,765 --> 00:10:00,766
Give me that.

137
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:06,772
Why do you have this photo of me?

138
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:08,024
It's so ugly!

139
00:10:08,107 --> 00:10:09,400
- Delete that.
- But it's cute.

140
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:10,693
Delete it already.

141
00:10:10,776 --> 00:10:11,736
No.

142
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:13,738
I'm going to upload this on your birthday.

143
00:10:14,655 --> 00:10:15,698
Here's another one.

144
00:10:17,408 --> 00:10:18,409
You know,

145
00:10:19,035 --> 00:10:21,287
let's just look
for someone here on campus.

146
00:10:22,079 --> 00:10:26,626
It looks like you really need
an organic encounter.

147
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:31,255
How about that one?

148
00:10:33,591 --> 00:10:34,925
Try to have some subtlety.

149
00:10:35,551 --> 00:10:36,677
Fine, never mind.

150
00:10:37,553 --> 00:10:39,764
That one is an irregular student
in our PE class.

151
00:10:39,847 --> 00:10:42,683
Her breath probably smells
worse than yours.

152
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,894
You can't be both stinky.

153
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:47,563
You really have no filter
on your mouth, do you?

154
00:11:03,496 --> 00:11:04,789
How about that one?

155
00:11:04,872 --> 00:11:06,749
- Miss, calm down.
- What happened?

156
00:11:06,832 --> 00:11:08,209
You're hopeless.

157
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:12,546
Bulots.

158
00:11:13,964 --> 00:11:16,509
Any dissenting opinion or opinions?

159
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:18,511
Attorney?

160
00:11:18,594 --> 00:11:19,428
Yes?

161
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:20,763
I think Janine has one.

162
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:24,058
All right, Ms. Mesina, let's hear it.

163
00:11:24,141 --> 00:11:25,518
- Let's go.
- Damn you.

164
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:34,985
The Writ of Kalikasan is…

165
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:37,613
Is a protection…

166
00:11:38,864 --> 00:11:40,241
Is…

167
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:42,701
I'm sorry, Attorney.

168
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:43,661
I'm sorry.

169
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:49,875
Ms. Mesina, this is just an intro to law.

170
00:11:49,959 --> 00:11:53,796
But when you proceed to law school,
the bar will be higher for you.

171
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:55,840
And just because you're my goddaughter

172
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:58,968
doesn't mean you get special treatment.

173
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:03,639
Attorney Mesina will be so disappointed.

174
00:12:05,599 --> 00:12:07,476
Reminder, everyone.

175
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:12,648
The 20 cases assigned for you
to read and make case digests of…

176
00:12:12,731 --> 00:12:14,400
No AI.

177
00:12:17,194 --> 00:12:18,362
That's it for today.

178
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:20,114
Class dismissed.

179
00:12:24,368 --> 00:12:26,036
Is it your first time donating blood?

180
00:12:27,204 --> 00:12:29,999
You know, it helps to listen to music.

181
00:12:50,227 --> 00:12:52,062
Sir, are you okay?

182
00:12:57,985 --> 00:13:01,030
"I expected more from you!"

183
00:13:02,239 --> 00:13:03,199
Good grief!

184
00:13:03,282 --> 00:13:05,784
Tone down the pressure a bit.

185
00:13:05,868 --> 00:13:07,745
What do they expect?

186
00:13:07,828 --> 00:13:11,165
That I had memorized the entire
1987 Constitution already?

187
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:13,959
I'm struggling enough as it is
with just the preamble.

188
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:17,796
What's so funny? Is that funny?

189
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:21,300
I'll punch your jaw.

190
00:13:23,719 --> 00:13:25,137
- Bulots.
- What?

191
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:28,224
Let's pretend it's your birthday today.

192
00:13:28,307 --> 00:13:29,767
But it's not my birthday yet.

193
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:30,976
I said let's pretend.

194
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,520
Oh, what should I do?

195
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:34,480
Who do you want to see?

196
00:13:34,563 --> 00:13:36,482
Of course…

197
00:13:36,565 --> 00:13:38,317
Kenzo baby.

198
00:13:39,235 --> 00:13:40,402
Love that.

199
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:43,113
Why did you ask?

200
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:50,621
What is this?

201
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:02,883
Grand Kenzo Day?

202
00:14:04,218 --> 00:14:05,386
Ouch!

203
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:06,887
Hey!

204
00:14:06,971 --> 00:14:07,888
Why?

205
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:09,390
What happened to you?

206
00:14:09,473 --> 00:14:10,724
I donated blood earlier.

207
00:14:10,808 --> 00:14:11,850
Hey.

208
00:14:11,934 --> 00:14:13,477
Look at you go, girl.

209
00:14:13,561 --> 00:14:15,062
You didn't collapse from the needle?

210
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:16,105
Not really.

211
00:14:18,315 --> 00:14:20,234
I just thought about the thing…

212
00:14:21,652 --> 00:14:22,945
The thing that calms me down.

213
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:24,947
You're so random.

214
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:31,829
Thank you.

215
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:36,125
You'll accompany me in commuting, right?

216
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:38,002
Do I even have a choice?

217
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:42,506
Thank you, Besh.

218
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:43,507
Love you.

219
00:14:46,176 --> 00:14:49,597
I'm finally going to see Kenzo.

220
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,610
Ma?

221
00:15:07,197 --> 00:15:08,407
Wait a second.

222
00:15:11,493 --> 00:15:12,369
Ma.

223
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:14,496
Your godmother called.

224
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:16,957
What?

225
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:19,501
She reported me to you?

226
00:15:19,585 --> 00:15:20,461
Huh?

227
00:15:20,544 --> 00:15:21,670
Report what?

228
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:23,422
Oh, nothing.

229
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:25,466
What did she say?

230
00:15:25,549 --> 00:15:27,259
<i>She's inviting us for dinner.</i>

231
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:29,094
<i>Maybe after your birthday?</i>

232
00:15:29,178 --> 00:15:33,182
Maybe she wants
to train you at her law firm.

233
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:35,059
<i>You probably impressed her.</i>

234
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:36,268
Yes, Ma.

235
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:38,812
She was very impressed with me.

236
00:15:38,896 --> 00:15:41,398
Anyway, why are you still up?

237
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:43,359
Just some late-night reading.

238
00:15:43,442 --> 00:15:46,528
Once you enter law school next year,

239
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:49,490
you practically won't be sleeping anymore.

240
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:52,993
<i>So while you still can,</i>
<i>you'd better sleep!</i>

241
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:54,411
Okay, Ma.

242
00:15:54,495 --> 00:15:56,163
I'm going to sleep now.

243
00:15:56,246 --> 00:15:57,331
Okay, good.

244
00:15:58,415 --> 00:15:59,833
Say hi to RR.

245
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:00,960
<i>I love you.</i>

246
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:02,252
Love you too, Ma.

247
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,004
Okay.

248
00:16:07,591 --> 00:16:08,467
Push.

249
00:16:12,304 --> 00:16:14,139
<i>I need to be careful now.</i>

250
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:16,725
<i>I know too much.</i>

251
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:18,936
<i>They won't leave me alone.</i>

252
00:16:19,019 --> 00:16:20,646
<i>Morning or night.</i>

253
00:16:20,729 --> 00:16:21,981
<i>Rain or shine.</i>

254
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:31,073
<i>But even if it's dangerous,</i>

255
00:16:31,156 --> 00:16:32,658
<i>Kenzo is always there.</i>

256
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:34,868
<i>Shit!</i>

257
00:16:35,536 --> 00:16:37,663
<i>My nose is stuffed up.</i>

258
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:49,758
You can keep it.

259
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:54,221
Why are you always getting yourself
caught in the rain?

260
00:16:54,304 --> 00:16:56,557
Because it takes you so long
to share your umbrella with me.

261
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:59,351
<i>Good Lord, Janine!</i>

262
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:01,061
<i>Is that really your answer?</i>

263
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:03,689
<i>Let the earth swallow me whole, please.</i>

264
00:17:03,772 --> 00:17:05,441
I've got you.

265
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:10,320
Just don't tell anyone who I really am.

266
00:17:12,614 --> 00:17:14,533
That you're the Undercover Love--

267
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:20,456
Be quiet about it.

268
00:17:21,081 --> 00:17:24,251
<i>So this is what it's like to have</i>
<i>an action hero for a boyfriend.</i>

269
00:17:24,334 --> 00:17:26,170
<i>As if! Boyfriend already?</i>

270
00:17:26,253 --> 00:17:27,755
<i>Let's calm down first!</i>

271
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:37,931
As long as I'm here…

272
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:41,935
I'll take care of you.

273
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:19,431
You're stinky, Pip.

274
00:18:26,563 --> 00:18:28,607
Is it full already?

275
00:18:28,690 --> 00:18:31,110
I'm in a hurry.

276
00:18:32,194 --> 00:18:33,362
Take my seat, ma'am.

277
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:36,073
- Thank you, young man.
- No problem, ma'am.

278
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:37,241
Thank you.

279
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:52,673
Are you trying to kill me?

280
00:18:53,423 --> 00:18:54,675
It was her.

281
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:57,761
Was it really her? No way.

282
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:05,060
Did all of these people chew that gum?

283
00:19:05,602 --> 00:19:08,480
- Of course. That's how much we love Kenzo.
- You're next.

284
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:10,816
Hello.

285
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:15,320
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

286
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:21,368
- So sorry.
- Are you okay here?

287
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:22,452
I'm okay now.

288
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:26,123
- I've got it.
- Hey.

289
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:27,291
What?

290
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:28,750
Huh?

291
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:30,252
Did you forget something?

292
00:19:30,335 --> 00:19:32,546
Of course not.

293
00:19:32,629 --> 00:19:34,548
It's impossible for me to forget this.

294
00:19:35,507 --> 00:19:37,050
- Enjoy.
- Take care, okay?

295
00:19:37,593 --> 00:19:38,677
Thank you.

296
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,853
Let's give Kenzo a round of applause.
We can't hear you!

297
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:49,855
Louder!

298
00:19:49,938 --> 00:19:51,315
Here! Louder!

299
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:53,734
Cheer louder! Louder!

300
00:19:53,817 --> 00:19:56,820
- Come on! Shout louder!
- Kenzo!

301
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:59,531
Louder! Make some noise!

302
00:19:59,615 --> 00:20:02,951
- Kenzo!
- Come on, that's it! Kenzo's on his way!

303
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:05,162
Everyone, let's go!

304
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:07,247
<i>Oh no. It's past 1:00 p.m.</i>

305
00:20:09,541 --> 00:20:12,002
Unbelievable. He's still not here.

306
00:20:12,085 --> 00:20:14,880
You know, ever since he stopped
collaborating with Ashley,

307
00:20:14,963 --> 00:20:17,299
Kenzo has become so unprofessional.

308
00:20:17,382 --> 00:20:18,508
That's true.

309
00:20:18,592 --> 00:20:21,178
It was really Ashley who carried Ash-Zo.

310
00:20:22,054 --> 00:20:24,848
Kenzo is not unprofessional.

311
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:30,103
You Ash-Zo shippers,
your ship name really suits you.

312
00:20:30,187 --> 00:20:32,231
All you do is bark.

313
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:33,482
Woof this, woof that.

314
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:35,442
You aren't even real Kenzo fans.

315
00:20:35,525 --> 00:20:37,069
Excuse me.

316
00:20:37,152 --> 00:20:38,403
We are real Kenzo fans.

317
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:40,405
Surely we're allowed to complain, right?

318
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:41,865
Because he's late.

319
00:20:41,949 --> 00:20:43,200
Complain?

320
00:20:43,283 --> 00:20:44,159
Why?

321
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:48,497
Did he complain to you when only ten of us
streamed his first song?

322
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:51,166
When only five of us
were watching his IG live,

323
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,542
did he complain to you?

324
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:53,585
No, right?

325
00:20:53,669 --> 00:20:57,089
Because you don't know him,
and you don't know what he's been through.

326
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:02,094
The girl is delusional.

327
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:06,682
What did you say?

328
00:21:06,765 --> 00:21:07,933
Hey, that's enough!

329
00:21:08,934 --> 00:21:10,686
Everybody, calm down.

330
00:21:14,231 --> 00:21:16,024
Why are you calling?
My interview is about to start.

331
00:21:16,108 --> 00:21:18,568
Just talk to me. I'm bored.

332
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:20,362
<i>Anyway, I have some gossip.</i>

333
00:21:20,445 --> 00:21:23,573
Earlier, I got into a fight
with two of Kenzo's bashers.

334
00:21:23,657 --> 00:21:24,783
So annoying!

335
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:28,704
And there's a PWD here who's faking it.

336
00:21:28,787 --> 00:21:31,123
Probably just to get Kenzo's attention.

337
00:21:31,206 --> 00:21:32,249
Hey.

338
00:21:32,332 --> 00:21:33,542
He might hear you.

339
00:21:33,625 --> 00:21:34,793
<i>And you know what?</i>

340
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:37,754
There's a mascot here.

341
00:21:37,838 --> 00:21:40,674
I really feel like this is Kenzo.

342
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:41,883
You know me.

343
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:43,969
I have a strong feeling
about these things.

344
00:21:44,052 --> 00:21:45,053
You're actually quite insensitive.

345
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:46,263
Huh? What was that?

346
00:21:46,346 --> 00:21:47,472
<i>Nothing.</i>

347
00:21:47,556 --> 00:21:50,142
I said you're beautiful, just deaf.

348
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:53,228
I know I'm beautiful. All right, fine.

349
00:21:53,312 --> 00:21:55,731
Whatever. Bye. Love you.

350
00:21:59,484 --> 00:22:00,485
Love you.

351
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:06,616
I really feel this is Kenzo.

352
00:22:16,251 --> 00:22:17,127
Hi.

353
00:22:18,545 --> 00:22:19,463
Kenzo?

354
00:22:20,047 --> 00:22:21,089
Is that you?

355
00:22:23,425 --> 00:22:25,886
You don't have to say anything.

356
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:27,929
It's just us here.

357
00:22:28,889 --> 00:22:32,559
I know you won't let your fans down.

358
00:22:33,393 --> 00:22:34,269
Right?

359
00:22:34,352 --> 00:22:36,063
Can I take a peek?

360
00:22:36,897 --> 00:22:37,898
Just a little.

361
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:40,025
I'll just peek. Just a little bit.

362
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:48,408
Sorry, sir. Sorry.

363
00:22:48,492 --> 00:22:49,951
Sorry.

364
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:52,370
Sorry.

365
00:22:52,913 --> 00:22:54,581
Sorry.

366
00:22:55,415 --> 00:22:57,125
<i>Good afternoon, Mr. Velasco.</i>

367
00:22:57,209 --> 00:22:58,335
Good afternoon, sir.

368
00:22:58,418 --> 00:23:01,671
I'm volunteering
for Guardians of Humanity.

369
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:03,381
<i>Can you hear me, Mr. Velasco?</i>

370
00:23:03,465 --> 00:23:04,382
Sir?

371
00:23:05,425 --> 00:23:06,885
<i>Mr. Velasco?</i>

372
00:23:06,968 --> 00:23:08,303
Sir, good af…

373
00:23:09,429 --> 00:23:10,680
Damn.

374
00:23:10,764 --> 00:23:13,350
Wow, this excitement is something else.

375
00:23:13,433 --> 00:23:16,394
You're all so strong,
so beautiful, and so handsome.

376
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:18,063
Wow.

377
00:23:18,688 --> 00:23:19,898
I'm so sorry.

378
00:23:19,981 --> 00:23:22,484
Kenzo won't be able to attend.

379
00:23:22,567 --> 00:23:23,610
Huh?

380
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:25,570
An emergency just came up.

381
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:28,406
But he sends his apologies,

382
00:23:28,490 --> 00:23:31,326
blessings, and all sorts of positivity.

383
00:23:31,409 --> 00:23:34,955
Yes, but for now, we need to leave. Yes.

384
00:23:35,038 --> 00:23:36,248
- The heck?
- Let's all stand up.

385
00:23:36,331 --> 00:23:38,708
- My butt is hurting.
- It's okay.

386
00:23:38,792 --> 00:23:39,876
- What the…
- What a waste.

387
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:42,087
- We've already turned off the aircon.
- I knew it!

388
00:23:42,170 --> 00:23:44,548
- You liar.
- You all need to leave.

389
00:23:44,631 --> 00:23:45,882
Please hurry up.

390
00:23:45,966 --> 00:23:47,509
I still have a date.

391
00:23:47,592 --> 00:23:51,138
You waited for hours,
and then he didn't even show up.

392
00:23:51,221 --> 00:23:52,514
Just unstan him already.

393
00:23:52,597 --> 00:23:55,016
You seem angrier than me.

394
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:56,476
I was the one who waited.

395
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:58,019
Hey, I waited too.

396
00:23:58,562 --> 00:23:59,771
I waited for you, you know.

397
00:23:59,855 --> 00:24:01,815
Hey, don't "hey" me.

398
00:24:01,898 --> 00:24:03,358
I didn't tell you to wait.

399
00:24:03,441 --> 00:24:06,111
I'm willing to wait
even if you don't say so.

400
00:24:06,194 --> 00:24:08,321
- You know that.
- I'm also willing to wait for Kenzo.

401
00:24:08,405 --> 00:24:09,906
Even if he doesn't say so.

402
00:24:10,574 --> 00:24:12,576
But that was still wrong, wasn't it?

403
00:24:12,659 --> 00:24:14,578
He made you wait for several hours.

404
00:24:17,998 --> 00:24:19,416
If it were me,

405
00:24:19,958 --> 00:24:21,168
I wouldn't do that.

406
00:24:22,752 --> 00:24:24,421
You already know that, don't you?

407
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:27,924
When I was in high school,
and now that I'm in college,

408
00:24:28,008 --> 00:24:31,261
Kenzo and his music
were the only ones there to comfort me

409
00:24:31,887 --> 00:24:36,474
because we're both hiding in the shadows

410
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:38,894
of our more famous parents.

411
00:24:40,770 --> 00:24:42,397
I can relate to that too.

412
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:46,401
I'm like a shadow following you.

413
00:24:46,484 --> 00:24:47,986
- Huh?
- Huh?

414
00:24:48,528 --> 00:24:49,905
Nothing. I said…

415
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:52,699
He doesn't even know how you feel.

416
00:24:52,782 --> 00:24:55,035
He doesn't even know you exist.

417
00:24:55,118 --> 00:24:57,287
That's just one-way, Bulots, okay?

418
00:24:57,370 --> 00:24:59,915
Okay, okay.

419
00:25:00,665 --> 00:25:03,835
Anyway, my only wish
for my birthday is that

420
00:25:04,377 --> 00:25:05,962
someday,

421
00:25:07,047 --> 00:25:09,007
he'll know that I exist.

422
00:25:09,090 --> 00:25:11,301
Even if he just reads my fanfic.

423
00:25:15,764 --> 00:25:16,932
Pip.

424
00:25:19,142 --> 00:25:20,310
Sleep here, okay?

425
00:25:24,898 --> 00:25:25,857
<i>Hi, guys!</i>

426
00:25:26,483 --> 00:25:28,735
<i>Long time no see.</i>

427
00:25:28,818 --> 00:25:29,903
<i>Okay.</i>

428
00:25:31,154 --> 00:25:32,781
<i>Let's read some comments first.</i>

429
00:25:34,282 --> 00:25:35,367
<i>"Idol,</i>

430
00:25:36,534 --> 00:25:39,287
<i>please read #MyUndercoverLove</i>

431
00:25:39,371 --> 00:25:41,706
<i>by diehard Kenzonatic fan."</i>

432
00:25:42,791 --> 00:25:44,459
"Written by

433
00:25:45,585 --> 00:25:47,754
TurtleLoverr06."

434
00:25:50,215 --> 00:25:51,299
<i>Wow!</i>

435
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:54,552
<i>"Best fanfic ever!"</i>

436
00:25:56,346 --> 00:25:57,514
<i>From…</i>

437
00:25:58,848 --> 00:26:00,141
<i>RawrRawr?</i>

438
00:26:00,225 --> 00:26:02,519
<i>Shout out to you, RawrRawr!</i>

439
00:26:02,602 --> 00:26:06,898
<i>And of course,</i>
<i>shout out to you too, TurtleLoverr06.</i>

440
00:26:06,982 --> 00:26:12,320
Actually, I think I can share it here
so that other fans can read it too.

441
00:26:12,404 --> 00:26:13,571
<i>There.</i>

442
00:26:14,239 --> 00:26:16,157
<i>Okay.</i>

443
00:26:16,241 --> 00:26:19,995
<i>Just let me know if TurtleLoverr06's</i>
My Undercover Love

444
00:26:20,078 --> 00:26:22,330
is any good.

445
00:26:43,518 --> 00:26:45,437
<i>Hi TurtleLover06, I just read your fanfic.</i>

446
00:26:45,520 --> 00:26:47,522
<i>I enjoyed it so much.</i>
<i>Maybe we can have dinner soon.</i>

447
00:26:50,483 --> 00:26:51,693
What the heck, Bulots?

448
00:26:52,360 --> 00:26:53,695
What's happening?

449
00:26:54,571 --> 00:26:56,114
I'm viral!

450
00:26:58,283 --> 00:26:59,951
My fanfic!

451
00:27:00,035 --> 00:27:00,952
It's viral now!

452
00:27:01,036 --> 00:27:03,663
And Kenzo messaged me!

453
00:27:03,747 --> 00:27:05,915
Oh my god!

454
00:27:09,919 --> 00:27:11,713
Let's go out! My treat.

455
00:27:11,796 --> 00:27:12,881
Come on!

456
00:27:15,550 --> 00:27:17,177
Damn it. I'm late.

457
00:27:18,428 --> 00:27:19,304
Wait!

458
00:27:21,765 --> 00:27:22,724
<i>Bulots.</i>

459
00:27:22,807 --> 00:27:26,186
Don't I always support you
in everything you do?

460
00:27:28,938 --> 00:27:31,441
Remember the volunteer program?

461
00:27:31,524 --> 00:27:32,942
The one that rejected me?

462
00:27:33,026 --> 00:27:34,694
They have a new opening.

463
00:27:35,445 --> 00:27:41,034
They're looking for volunteers
to train abroad.

464
00:27:41,785 --> 00:27:42,911
Abroad?

465
00:27:43,995 --> 00:27:45,038
What do you mean "mmm"?

466
00:27:45,622 --> 00:27:48,249
They said I just need to attend

467
00:27:48,333 --> 00:27:50,627
that emergency response training course.

468
00:27:50,710 --> 00:27:54,297
And one of the requirements
is a recommendation letter

469
00:27:54,381 --> 00:27:57,050
from a university representative.

470
00:27:57,133 --> 00:27:59,219
Aren't you in the Student Council?

471
00:27:59,302 --> 00:28:01,846
Maybe you could help out.
You're my favorite writer after all.

472
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:06,810
Just a letter?

473
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:10,146
All right.

474
00:28:10,230 --> 00:28:11,147
I'll help you,

475
00:28:11,231 --> 00:28:13,525
but on one condition.

476
00:28:13,608 --> 00:28:14,859
What?

477
00:28:14,943 --> 00:28:17,987
Please don't call me Bulots
in front of Kenzo.

478
00:28:18,071 --> 00:28:19,697
Please.

479
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:21,157
But it's so cute.

480
00:28:21,908 --> 00:28:23,118
Kenzo?

481
00:28:23,201 --> 00:28:24,577
KenBul.

482
00:28:24,661 --> 00:28:25,870
KenBul?

483
00:28:26,704 --> 00:28:27,789
KenkenBul.

484
00:28:29,666 --> 00:28:31,501
Don't you dare embarrass me!

485
00:28:32,127 --> 00:28:33,795
I won't write you the letter.

486
00:28:34,546 --> 00:28:35,964
But it's good.

487
00:28:36,047 --> 00:28:37,006
Kenzo.

488
00:28:37,549 --> 00:28:38,550
KenkenBul.

489
00:28:48,852 --> 00:28:51,062
TurtleLoverr06.

490
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:55,942
I told you.

491
00:28:56,651 --> 00:28:57,736
Just call me Janine.

492
00:29:01,614 --> 00:29:02,449
Kenzo.

493
00:29:08,455 --> 00:29:09,914
Janine.

494
00:29:09,998 --> 00:29:11,875
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

495
00:29:15,545 --> 00:29:16,588
Kenzo, man.

496
00:29:20,216 --> 00:29:21,259
RR.

497
00:29:21,342 --> 00:29:22,761
Nice to meet you.

498
00:29:22,844 --> 00:29:23,845
You're late.

499
00:29:26,473 --> 00:29:27,640
His hand is wet.

500
00:29:28,433 --> 00:29:32,687
And here's the deconstructed
sweet potato reduced to a foam.

501
00:29:32,771 --> 00:29:33,605
Enjoy.

502
00:29:34,564 --> 00:29:36,441
Is there no real food here?

503
00:29:36,524 --> 00:29:38,026
Good thing I already ate.

504
00:29:39,819 --> 00:29:41,404
Anyways, Janine.

505
00:29:42,363 --> 00:29:46,868
The reason I wanted to meet with you
is that my management

506
00:29:46,951 --> 00:29:49,788
is thinking about various projects.

507
00:29:49,871 --> 00:29:51,915
And I told them that

508
00:29:51,998 --> 00:29:54,167
I wanted to collaborate with a fan.

509
00:29:54,250 --> 00:29:57,504
I am your number one fan.

510
00:30:02,342 --> 00:30:03,426
Hey, Bulots.

511
00:30:05,053 --> 00:30:06,304
That's a bit harsh.

512
00:30:07,263 --> 00:30:08,348
Bulots?

513
00:30:08,431 --> 00:30:10,308
Your nicknames for each other are so cute.

514
00:30:11,184 --> 00:30:13,186
- Why Bulots?
- Because--

515
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:16,606
Short for…

516
00:30:17,357 --> 00:30:19,025
"beauty lots."

517
00:30:19,108 --> 00:30:20,485
Lots of beauty.

518
00:30:20,568 --> 00:30:22,695
That's all. Just being beautiful.

519
00:30:24,781 --> 00:30:27,075
I'm really beautiful, right? Right, Pip?

520
00:30:28,034 --> 00:30:29,244
Pip?

521
00:30:29,327 --> 00:30:30,453
Why Pip?

522
00:30:30,537 --> 00:30:32,580
Because you're the fifth
among your siblings?

523
00:30:36,835 --> 00:30:37,961
Am I right?

524
00:30:38,753 --> 00:30:40,839
Pip, because you were 15 minutes late.

525
00:30:40,922 --> 00:30:42,298
Or it could be 50-50.

526
00:30:42,382 --> 00:30:44,509
50-50 on whether you'd show up or not.

527
00:30:44,592 --> 00:30:48,054
Please bear with my best friend here.

528
00:30:48,137 --> 00:30:49,347
He's quite the joker.

529
00:30:49,430 --> 00:30:50,849
Nice.

530
00:30:50,932 --> 00:30:52,141
You're really good.

531
00:30:52,225 --> 00:30:53,518
Wait, best friend.

532
00:30:53,601 --> 00:30:55,103
Did I hear that right?

533
00:30:55,186 --> 00:30:56,229
I thought you were--

534
00:30:56,312 --> 00:30:57,605
A couple?

535
00:30:57,689 --> 00:30:58,815
No.

536
00:30:58,898 --> 00:30:59,941
Just best friends.

537
00:31:01,317 --> 00:31:02,485
Excuse me.

538
00:31:03,695 --> 00:31:05,405
Salmon at the center.

539
00:31:05,488 --> 00:31:08,449
What we need is a celebration of things
that are often overlooked.

540
00:31:09,117 --> 00:31:12,328
Things that are
often forgotten or unnoticed.

541
00:31:12,412 --> 00:31:13,746
Green peas.

542
00:31:14,330 --> 00:31:17,917
It's green peas reimagined,
reinvented, reborn.

543
00:31:18,001 --> 00:31:19,294
Enjoy.

