<i>The movie is five hours long. Damn. Sorry.</i>

820
00:45:25,264 --> 00:45:27,391
- Miss!
- Oh, Ma'am Sue.

821
00:45:27,474 --> 00:45:29,101
Ma'am, sorry.

822
00:45:29,184 --> 00:45:31,645
We're closed right now
for a private event.

823
00:45:31,728 --> 00:45:33,355
Just two bottles, please.

824
00:45:33,439 --> 00:45:35,274
- Please, miss.
- Two bottles?

825
00:45:36,442 --> 00:45:37,484
But, ma'am…

826
00:45:37,568 --> 00:45:38,986
Please!

827
00:45:39,069 --> 00:45:40,112
Hey!

828
00:45:40,195 --> 00:45:41,071
Oh!

829
00:45:41,155 --> 00:45:42,364
You look like
you're dressed up for church.

830
00:45:42,448 --> 00:45:43,615
Why are you all dressed up?

831
00:45:43,699 --> 00:45:44,992
Oh.

832
00:45:45,075 --> 00:45:47,035
And you're at a local diner.

833
00:45:47,828 --> 00:45:48,704
May I?

834
00:45:49,246 --> 00:45:50,080
Sure.

835
00:45:53,417 --> 00:45:57,713
So, either A,

836
00:45:58,422 --> 00:45:59,798
you got dumped.

837
00:45:59,882 --> 00:46:01,383
B,

838
00:46:02,176 --> 00:46:03,760
you got stood up, right?

839
00:46:05,804 --> 00:46:07,181
Letter B.

840
00:46:07,264 --> 00:46:08,140
Final answer.

841
00:46:08,849 --> 00:46:10,601
But why here?

842
00:46:12,394 --> 00:46:13,770
Why here?

843
00:46:15,772 --> 00:46:18,484
Because this is
where I first realized that…

844
00:46:19,735 --> 00:46:20,569
That…

845
00:46:21,862 --> 00:46:22,946
That I love her.

846
00:46:25,282 --> 00:46:28,952
The girl from the gym?

847
00:46:30,078 --> 00:46:31,163
Okay.

848
00:46:31,246 --> 00:46:33,290
- When we had problems--
- Here you go, sir.

849
00:46:33,373 --> 00:46:35,375
- One bucket.
- Thank you, miss.

850
00:46:35,459 --> 00:46:39,171
When we had family problems,
she brought me here.

851
00:46:39,254 --> 00:46:41,548
Did she give you advice?

852
00:46:42,090 --> 00:46:42,925
No.

853
00:46:43,008 --> 00:46:45,511
She just kept making me laugh all night.

854
00:46:45,594 --> 00:46:47,221
Even if her jokes were corny,

855
00:46:47,304 --> 00:46:48,555
she really got me.

856
00:46:49,348 --> 00:46:52,100
I even forgot I had problems back then.

857
00:46:52,726 --> 00:46:53,560
Okay.

858
00:46:54,102 --> 00:46:55,395
Here.

859
00:46:57,940 --> 00:46:59,066
What's that?

860
00:46:59,816 --> 00:47:02,277
I carved this when she fell asleep.

861
00:47:02,361 --> 00:47:05,405
I carved it because I didn't want
to forget that night.

862
00:47:06,740 --> 00:47:08,200
I didn't want to forget

863
00:47:08,742 --> 00:47:11,578
the moment I found the person
who would make me happy.

864
00:47:23,757 --> 00:47:26,093
Miss. Hey. It's over.

865
00:47:26,176 --> 00:47:27,427
Oh, it's already over.

866
00:47:32,516 --> 00:47:33,559
It's already 2 a.m.

867
00:47:34,810 --> 00:47:35,811
Oh no!

868
00:47:39,982 --> 00:47:42,442
- Excuse me, please. Sorry.
- Wait!

869
00:47:44,152 --> 00:47:45,028
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

870
00:47:50,909 --> 00:47:53,912
Hey, RR, think about
what I told you earlier.

871
00:47:53,996 --> 00:47:57,291
We need volunteers at the Fire Department.

872
00:47:59,251 --> 00:48:00,127
I feel cold.

873
00:48:01,086 --> 00:48:02,588
Oh. Here.

874
00:48:02,671 --> 00:48:04,464
Good thing I'm prepared.

875
00:48:08,427 --> 00:48:09,428
Thank you.

876
00:48:12,681 --> 00:48:13,640
Hey!

877
00:48:13,724 --> 00:48:15,392
There's your best friend.

878
00:48:22,649 --> 00:48:23,609
Hello.

879
00:48:25,611 --> 00:48:26,778
Pip.

880
00:48:27,863 --> 00:48:29,615
I feel cold too, you know.

881
00:48:30,699 --> 00:48:31,658
Take it.

882
00:48:34,119 --> 00:48:34,995
Sue.

883
00:48:35,912 --> 00:48:37,164
That's hers.

884
00:48:37,706 --> 00:48:40,250
Okay. Go, go, go.

885
00:48:40,917 --> 00:48:41,752
Go.

886
00:48:42,669 --> 00:48:43,629
It's really cold.

887
00:48:52,971 --> 00:48:54,806
Gym expert, right?

888
00:48:55,515 --> 00:48:56,433
Slash.

889
00:48:57,059 --> 00:48:59,353
Environmental activist.

890
00:48:59,436 --> 00:49:00,270
Slash.

891
00:49:00,354 --> 00:49:01,647
Published author.

892
00:49:01,730 --> 00:49:02,981
And slash.

893
00:49:04,066 --> 00:49:05,984
You seem to have it all, huh?

894
00:49:07,486 --> 00:49:08,612
Right, Pip?

895
00:49:10,197 --> 00:49:12,199
By the way, this is Sue.

896
00:49:12,783 --> 00:49:14,701
- And this is Janine.
- Hi.

897
00:49:14,785 --> 00:49:16,411
Nice to meet you.

898
00:49:17,245 --> 00:49:19,289
Pip? Why do you call him Pip?

899
00:49:20,123 --> 00:49:21,541
Isn't his name RR?

900
00:49:21,625 --> 00:49:24,503
They thought I was mute
back in elementary.

901
00:49:25,962 --> 00:49:27,381
Can I call you Pip too?

902
00:49:27,464 --> 00:49:28,674
- Sure!
- No!

903
00:49:29,383 --> 00:49:30,300
Hey!

904
00:49:30,384 --> 00:49:32,094
I'm the only one
who can call you that, right?

905
00:49:32,177 --> 00:49:33,220
That's just ours.

906
00:49:33,845 --> 00:49:35,555
Anyways…

907
00:49:35,639 --> 00:49:37,933
I was inviting RR

908
00:49:38,016 --> 00:49:41,937
to join me in the BFP volunteer program.

909
00:49:42,020 --> 00:49:43,271
BFP?

910
00:49:44,022 --> 00:49:45,065
Firefighter?

911
00:49:46,066 --> 00:49:47,275
That's dangerous.

912
00:49:47,818 --> 00:49:49,027
And hey.

913
00:49:49,111 --> 00:49:51,571
Didn't you tell me
you'd focus on your midterms?

914
00:49:51,655 --> 00:49:54,658
As for my organization,

915
00:49:55,283 --> 00:49:58,537
they send volunteers to Sudan.

916
00:49:58,620 --> 00:50:00,288
- Sudan?
- Yes.

917
00:50:00,372 --> 00:50:02,916
That would be good training for RR.

918
00:50:02,999 --> 00:50:04,292
Yeah.

919
00:50:04,376 --> 00:50:07,170
You're a member of
Guardians of Humanity, right?

920
00:50:07,254 --> 00:50:08,922
Not just a member.

921
00:50:09,756 --> 00:50:12,759
One of the Board of Directors.

922
00:50:15,470 --> 00:50:19,099
No wonder I'm so bored with you now.

923
00:50:19,182 --> 00:50:20,434
Huh?

924
00:50:21,518 --> 00:50:23,228
How about your studies?

925
00:50:24,312 --> 00:50:25,814
That's a good opportunity for RR.

926
00:50:25,897 --> 00:50:30,652
We need someone who's as passionate as RR.

927
00:50:30,736 --> 00:50:31,737
Passionate?

928
00:50:32,612 --> 00:50:33,447
Why?

929
00:50:34,322 --> 00:50:37,576
Are you lifelong friends?
Do you have childhood memories together?

930
00:50:38,368 --> 00:50:39,619
Hey.

931
00:50:39,703 --> 00:50:40,871
You just met.

932
00:50:40,954 --> 00:50:43,540
- Hey.
- His studies won't stop.

933
00:50:43,623 --> 00:50:47,544
I mean, it will only just take one year,

934
00:50:47,627 --> 00:50:49,629
and then I think

935
00:50:50,422 --> 00:50:52,716
he will do so good there.

936
00:50:53,550 --> 00:50:57,179
Anyways, RR told me.

937
00:50:57,262 --> 00:50:59,890
You watched the special screening

938
00:50:59,973 --> 00:51:02,642
of the new Pascal Seswa film.

939
00:51:03,268 --> 00:51:06,313
- I'm such a fan!
- Yes!

940
00:51:06,396 --> 00:51:09,608
And you know, Kenzo was really sweet.

941
00:51:09,691 --> 00:51:11,568
Kenzo?

942
00:51:11,651 --> 00:51:14,446
He even invited me to dinner
after we watched the movie.

943
00:51:14,529 --> 00:51:15,489
Dinner?

944
00:51:17,073 --> 00:51:18,492
It's almost three o'clock!

945
00:51:18,575 --> 00:51:20,494
Oh, I mean,

946
00:51:20,577 --> 00:51:22,579
midnight snack!

947
00:51:22,662 --> 00:51:25,540
Or maybe breakfast.
Just pick which one you like.

948
00:51:25,624 --> 00:51:27,334
Good thing you didn't have an allergy.

949
00:51:27,417 --> 00:51:29,044
No, I didn't.

950
00:51:29,127 --> 00:51:32,464
Because there were paramedics
on standby for me.

951
00:51:33,173 --> 00:51:34,883
That's how sweet he is.

952
00:51:34,966 --> 00:51:36,676
That's so nice!

953
00:51:36,760 --> 00:51:38,386
So nice, right?

954
00:51:38,470 --> 00:51:40,430
- That's so nice! Wow!
- Oh my god!

955
00:51:40,514 --> 00:51:42,432
- It's really nice!
- It's so nice!

956
00:51:42,516 --> 00:51:44,643
It's really nice!

957
00:51:44,726 --> 00:51:46,436
- So nice!
- So nice!

958
00:51:46,520 --> 00:51:49,731
- Nice!
- Right? It's really nice!

959
00:51:51,399 --> 00:51:53,443
So? Is she your girlfriend now?

960
00:51:55,612 --> 00:51:57,823
I just met her.
How can she be my girlfriend?

961
00:51:58,990 --> 00:52:00,075
Is there a chance?

962
00:52:00,784 --> 00:52:01,660
We do.

963
00:52:09,084 --> 00:52:10,377
Were you there all night?

964
00:52:11,002 --> 00:52:11,878
Yes.

965
00:52:12,963 --> 00:52:14,214
Why do you have so many questions?

966
00:52:14,297 --> 00:52:18,593
Is it wrong to be curious
about my best friend's future partner?

967
00:52:21,179 --> 00:52:22,430
She's mature.

968
00:52:23,473 --> 00:52:24,683
I'll give her that.

969
00:52:25,308 --> 00:52:27,269
Maybe that's what you need.

970
00:52:27,352 --> 00:52:28,854
You're right.

971
00:52:28,937 --> 00:52:30,146
She's mature.

972
00:52:30,981 --> 00:52:33,149
Unlike you, who's very immature.

973
00:52:40,615 --> 00:52:41,449
What are you doing?

974
00:52:42,075 --> 00:52:43,076
Why?

975
00:52:44,160 --> 00:52:46,580
Can't I be sweet with my best friend?

976
00:52:47,956 --> 00:52:51,084
Are you afraid you might lose me
because of her?

977
00:52:53,336 --> 00:52:54,671
That I'll lose time for you?

978
00:52:55,589 --> 00:52:56,756
Killjoy.

979
00:53:01,761 --> 00:53:03,138
But yes,

980
00:53:03,221 --> 00:53:04,890
as selfish as it may sound.

981
00:53:08,768 --> 00:53:09,895
Good thing you know.

982
00:53:10,937 --> 00:53:12,647
You're very selfish.

983
00:53:12,731 --> 00:53:16,902
At least now you know my favorite seafood.

984
00:53:16,985 --> 00:53:18,153
Huh?

985
00:53:18,778 --> 00:53:20,864
Shellfish!

986
00:53:22,365 --> 00:53:23,825
You're corny.

987
00:53:23,909 --> 00:53:25,410
Yeah, idiot.

988
00:53:26,077 --> 00:53:27,287
You're smiling.

989
00:53:27,370 --> 00:53:29,998
Your nostrils are flaring.

990
00:53:35,295 --> 00:53:36,171
Pip.

991
00:53:38,089 --> 00:53:39,549
Come study with me, okay?

992
00:54:00,320 --> 00:54:01,655
<i>Where are you?</i>

993
00:54:03,740 --> 00:54:05,659
<i>I'm doing volunteer work with the BFP.</i>

994
00:54:23,093 --> 00:54:24,886
<i>It's better without one.</i>

995
00:54:24,970 --> 00:54:26,972
<i>Why does her lover have two Rs?</i>

996
00:54:27,055 --> 00:54:29,099
<i>Is it just a style</i>
<i>or does it have a meaning?</i>

997
00:54:30,433 --> 00:54:32,936
<i>Where is the next part?</i>

998
00:54:33,019 --> 00:54:34,396
<i>Waiting for the next chapter!</i>

999
00:54:34,479 --> 00:54:36,398
<i>I'll name my kid after Kenzo.</i>

1000
00:54:45,657 --> 00:54:49,327
<i>Hey, Janine, about last night.</i>
<i>Really sorry.</i>

1001
00:54:50,537 --> 00:54:55,166
<i>Don't worry. I really liked the movie.</i>
<i>So it's okay.</i>

1002
00:55:11,558 --> 00:55:13,685
<i>Chapter 31.</i>

1003
00:55:13,768 --> 00:55:17,147
<i>Kenzo promised I'd be safe</i>
<i>as long as he's there.</i>

1004
00:55:17,230 --> 00:55:18,565
<i>But why does it feel like this?</i>

1005
00:55:19,232 --> 00:55:22,610
<i>It's like something inside me has changed.</i>

1006
00:55:23,236 --> 00:55:25,280
<i>Even though I know Kenzo is there,</i>

1007
00:55:25,363 --> 00:55:27,490
<i>it feels like I'm looking</i>
<i>for someone else.</i>

1008
00:55:28,283 --> 00:55:29,743
<i>There's someone else</i>

1009
00:55:29,826 --> 00:55:30,952
<i>I want to see.</i>

1010
00:55:31,828 --> 00:55:34,456
<i>Someone familiar?</i>

1011
00:55:35,957 --> 00:55:37,625
<i>I feel weak.</i>

1012
00:55:37,709 --> 00:55:39,044
<i>I'm getting dizzy.</i>

1013
00:55:41,629 --> 00:55:42,756
<i>Poison?</i>

1014
00:55:43,715 --> 00:55:45,508
<i>Did they poison my water?</i>

1015
00:56:04,611 --> 00:56:05,487
<i>Kenzo?</i>

1016
00:56:07,989 --> 00:56:08,865
<i>Kenzo?</i>

1017
00:56:10,575 --> 00:56:11,451
<i>Pip?</i>

1018
00:56:13,369 --> 00:56:14,245
<i>Pip?</i>

1019
00:56:16,956 --> 00:56:17,832
<i>Pip?</i>

1020
00:56:18,833 --> 00:56:19,709
<i>Kenzo?</i>

1021
00:56:29,302 --> 00:56:30,178
<i>Ken…</i>

1022
00:56:39,687 --> 00:56:40,688
Pip?

1023
00:56:45,860 --> 00:56:47,362
Sis, are you okay?

1024
00:56:48,404 --> 00:56:49,280
I'm okay.

1025
00:56:50,824 --> 00:56:51,658
Okay.

1026
00:56:51,741 --> 00:56:55,578
Does this sulking of yours have something
to do with the loss of your shadow?

1027
00:56:56,871 --> 00:56:58,706
Because if you don't like him, it's okay.

1028
00:56:58,790 --> 00:57:01,126
Like if you turned him down,
what do you call that?

1029
00:57:01,209 --> 00:57:02,168
Rejected?

1030
00:57:02,252 --> 00:57:05,213
How can I reject him
when he didn't even court me?

1031
00:57:05,296 --> 00:57:06,339
So dramatic.

1032
00:57:06,422 --> 00:57:08,091
Okay, so he's moving on from you.

1033
00:57:08,174 --> 00:57:11,094
How can he move on
when we were never together?

1034
00:57:11,177 --> 00:57:15,431
You don't have to be exes
to move on from someone.

1035
00:57:15,974 --> 00:57:17,517
Why? Is he courting someone else?

1036
00:57:19,144 --> 00:57:21,020
What are you even saying, Jess?

1037
00:57:21,104 --> 00:57:21,938
Okay.

1038
00:57:22,564 --> 00:57:24,232
Because you guys are so, so close.

1039
00:57:24,315 --> 00:57:25,817
And I get that, okay?

1040
00:57:25,900 --> 00:57:27,277
Like he's always there.

1041
00:57:27,360 --> 00:57:30,905
But sometimes,
you just need to take a step back.

1042
00:57:31,781 --> 00:57:34,200
So that you can really see him.

1043
00:57:34,284 --> 00:57:36,995
Because you only get to see him now

1044
00:57:37,078 --> 00:57:38,997
because he's slowly walking away.

1045
00:57:39,080 --> 00:57:41,541
But if I were you,

1046
00:57:41,624 --> 00:57:44,043
I wouldn't even let him walk any further.

1047
00:57:44,711 --> 00:57:47,755
Because before you know it, he'll be gone.
He'll be so far away.

1048
00:57:47,839 --> 00:57:49,215
So, so far away.

1049
00:57:49,299 --> 00:57:50,925
So far away?

1050
00:57:51,009 --> 00:57:52,218
So far away.

1051
00:58:02,770 --> 00:58:05,899
<i>Pip, when is the BFP training?</i>

1052
00:58:09,944 --> 00:58:11,404
You're into boxing now?

1053
00:58:12,155 --> 00:58:13,323
- Yeah.
- Isn't it in QC?

1054
00:58:13,406 --> 00:58:15,116
Really? So you're doing it regularly?

1055
00:58:17,785 --> 00:58:19,704
Hi!

1056
00:58:20,246 --> 00:58:22,874
I'm happy you decided to join us, Janine.

1057
00:58:23,541 --> 00:58:24,417
Are we close?

1058
00:58:25,043 --> 00:58:25,919
Huh?

1059
00:58:26,669 --> 00:58:28,671
Nothing. I said…

1060
00:58:28,755 --> 00:58:30,673
I'm happy to be here.

1061
00:58:31,299 --> 00:58:32,258
That's nice.

1062
00:58:33,593 --> 00:58:35,178
Hasn't it started yet?

1063
00:58:37,180 --> 00:58:38,056
Hold this.

1064
00:58:38,973 --> 00:58:40,975
Let's go! Let's start!

1065
00:58:41,059 --> 00:58:43,311
- Hey! This is embarrassing!
- Come on!

1066
00:58:43,394 --> 00:58:44,395
Come on!

1067
00:58:47,941 --> 00:58:49,817
Do you need help with your visa?

1068
00:58:51,486 --> 00:58:53,321
Visa for where?

1069
00:58:53,404 --> 00:58:54,656
Okay. Next!

1070
00:58:54,739 --> 00:58:56,157
- Next. Okay.
- Next!

1071
00:58:57,867 --> 00:58:58,993
Pip,

1072
00:58:59,077 --> 00:59:00,286
what is the visa for?

1073
00:59:01,412 --> 00:59:04,207
For our volunteer work in Sudan.

1074
00:59:04,290 --> 00:59:05,625
Left.

1075
00:59:06,417 --> 00:59:08,795
This is a major life decision.

1076
00:59:09,462 --> 00:59:11,047
And no one's going to tell me?

1077
00:59:11,130 --> 00:59:13,424
He's an injured person, Janine.
He can't talk to you.

1078
00:59:13,508 --> 00:59:14,425
Left.

1079
00:59:14,509 --> 00:59:17,387
He'll really get injured
if he doesn't answer me.

1080
00:59:17,470 --> 00:59:19,347
- This is embarrassing!
- Left.

1081
00:59:20,431 --> 00:59:21,307
Right!

1082
00:59:21,933 --> 00:59:22,809
Left!

1083
00:59:23,643 --> 00:59:24,644
Right!

1084
00:59:25,687 --> 00:59:28,147
Just stay steady, okay?
We're almost there, Pip.

1085
00:59:28,231 --> 00:59:29,148
Pip?

1086
00:59:30,775 --> 00:59:33,570
Pip? Really?
I'm the only one allowed to call you that.

1087
00:59:33,653 --> 00:59:35,071
Focus, Janine.

1088
00:59:35,154 --> 00:59:36,197
Janine?

1089
00:59:36,739 --> 00:59:39,117
What, you don't want
to call me Bulots anymore?

1090
00:59:39,200 --> 00:59:41,244
Before, you didn't want
to be called Bulots.

1091
00:59:41,327 --> 00:59:42,662
Now you want it?

1092
00:59:43,663 --> 00:59:44,539
You're confusing, sis.

1093
00:59:44,622 --> 00:59:45,707
Sis?

1094
00:59:45,790 --> 00:59:47,500
There were other people before.

1095
00:59:48,251 --> 00:59:50,295
It's different
because your Kenzo wasn't there.

1096
00:59:50,378 --> 00:59:52,130
So you're getting back at me?

1097
00:59:53,089 --> 00:59:54,632
Why would I get back at you?

1098
00:59:56,718 --> 00:59:58,428
- You're a mess.
- Whatever.

1099
00:59:58,511 --> 01:00:00,555
No one else can call you Pip.

1100
01:00:00,638 --> 01:00:02,682
Let's go, Pip and friend!

1101
01:00:04,434 --> 01:00:06,144
Damn it! Janine!

1102
01:00:06,227 --> 01:00:08,021
- Stop it!
- What's your problem?

1103
01:00:08,104 --> 01:00:08,980
Stop!

1104
01:00:10,023 --> 01:00:11,566
- Janine!
- What?

1105
01:00:12,442 --> 01:00:13,860
What's going on with you?

1106
01:00:15,278 --> 01:00:16,112
Okay.

1107
01:00:18,114 --> 01:00:19,282
Sorry, sir.

1108
01:00:19,907 --> 01:00:21,075
It's all right.

1109
01:00:23,453 --> 01:00:24,579
You know that…

1110
01:00:25,121 --> 01:00:26,789
“Pip” is ours.

1111
01:00:27,582 --> 01:00:28,458
Wait.

1112
01:00:29,000 --> 01:00:30,835
Why does it feel like
you're the one sulking?

1113
01:00:30,918 --> 01:00:31,961
Shouldn't it be me?

1114
01:00:33,379 --> 01:00:36,424
Because you didn't even tell me
you're really going to Sudan.

1115
01:00:36,507 --> 01:00:38,134
I'm your best friend.

1116
01:00:38,217 --> 01:00:39,469
Let me remind you of that.

1117
01:00:40,970 --> 01:00:42,472
I'm still just applying.

1118
01:00:43,598 --> 01:00:45,099
I'm not even sure yet.

1119
01:00:45,933 --> 01:00:47,894
A lot can still happen.

1120
01:00:47,977 --> 01:00:49,646
Are you really ready?

1121
01:00:50,772 --> 01:00:52,607
Have you completed your training?

1122
01:00:53,941 --> 01:00:56,319
Do you know how to speak their language?

1123
01:00:56,944 --> 01:00:57,945
What do you call it?

1124
01:00:58,613 --> 01:01:00,573
Sudanians?

1125
01:01:02,200 --> 01:01:03,201
Sudanese?

1126
01:01:04,160 --> 01:01:05,036
Oh.

1127
01:01:06,162 --> 01:01:07,664
What if someone asks for help?

1128
01:01:07,747 --> 01:01:10,708
As a first responder, what will you do?

1129
01:01:16,422 --> 01:01:17,548
Sorry.

1130
01:01:17,632 --> 01:01:19,175
How can I help?

1131
01:01:19,258 --> 01:01:20,968
No English!

1132
01:01:21,052 --> 01:01:24,430
No, no, no! No English!

1133
01:01:30,144 --> 01:01:32,105
What happened, madam? How can I help?

1134
01:01:32,188 --> 01:01:33,690
Are you stupid?

1135
01:01:33,773 --> 01:01:35,525
They don't know how to speak English.

1136
01:01:37,193 --> 01:01:39,696
Just say what you want to say.

1137
01:01:39,779 --> 01:01:41,322
If you don't want me to leave,
just say it.

1138
01:01:41,406 --> 01:01:44,701
I'm just making sure
you're really ready to leave.

1139
01:01:44,784 --> 01:01:46,786
You seem so eager.

1140
01:01:46,869 --> 01:01:48,871
What if someone drowns?

1141
01:01:48,955 --> 01:01:50,415
Do you know how to do CPR?

1142
01:01:53,418 --> 01:01:55,128
Madam!

1143
01:01:55,211 --> 01:01:58,339
Call emergency services! Right away!

1144
01:01:58,423 --> 01:01:59,632
You're really stupid, huh?

1145
01:01:59,716 --> 01:02:01,634
I said they don't know
how to speak English!

1146
01:02:05,054 --> 01:02:06,431
Madam!

1147
01:02:15,690 --> 01:02:17,567
Here, idiot. Here.

1148
01:02:18,776 --> 01:02:19,777
Here.

1149
01:02:56,063 --> 01:02:56,898
Sorry.

1150
01:02:56,981 --> 01:02:58,649
Sorry too.

1151
01:02:59,275 --> 01:03:00,276
- For what?
- For what?

1152
01:03:05,072 --> 01:03:05,948
Pip?

1153
01:03:07,325 --> 01:03:08,993
Why don't you just sleep here?

1154
01:03:30,640 --> 01:03:31,474
It's cold.

1155
01:03:36,687 --> 01:03:37,814
Excuse me.

1156
01:04:00,878 --> 01:04:02,255
Are you sleepy?

1157
01:04:03,297 --> 01:04:04,382
Not yet.

1158
01:04:43,796 --> 01:04:47,425
<i>I don't know what happened</i>
<i>after I lost consciousness.</i>

1159
01:04:47,508 --> 01:04:48,843
<i>All I know is…</i>

1160
01:04:49,468 --> 01:04:52,722
<i>I just woke up,</i>
<i>and Kenzo was already with me.</i>

1161
01:04:52,805 --> 01:04:54,307
Relax.

1162
01:04:54,390 --> 01:04:55,600
<i>Once again,</i>

1163
01:04:56,601 --> 01:04:57,602
<i>he saved me.</i>

1164
01:04:57,685 --> 01:05:00,354
Looks like you drank a strong poison.

1165
01:05:01,689 --> 01:05:03,774
You are calling me by a different name.

1166
01:05:04,400 --> 01:05:05,401
Thank you.

1167
01:05:07,153 --> 01:05:09,405
You have saved my life many times.

1168
01:05:10,031 --> 01:05:11,657
Didn't I tell you that

1169
01:05:12,950 --> 01:05:14,702
as long as I'm here,

1170
01:05:14,785 --> 01:05:16,287
you are safe?

1171
01:05:17,246 --> 01:05:19,081
<i>Wait, what's happening?</i>

1172
01:05:19,165 --> 01:05:20,416
<i>Oh my gosh.</i>

1173
01:05:21,167 --> 01:05:23,210
<i>I've been waiting for this my whole life.</i>

1174
01:05:24,670 --> 01:05:26,422
<i>But why does it feel like this?</i>

1175
01:05:26,505 --> 01:05:27,965
<i>Something feels wrong.</i>

1176
01:05:28,925 --> 01:05:30,801
<i>Isn't this supposed to be my fantasy?</i>

1177
01:05:31,469 --> 01:05:32,720
Sorry, Kenzo.

1178
01:05:35,056 --> 01:05:36,057
I'm sorry.

1179
01:05:37,141 --> 01:05:38,309
Why?

1180
01:05:39,226 --> 01:05:40,895
I don't know, okay?

1181
01:05:41,562 --> 01:05:43,564
But one thing I'm sure of

1182
01:05:44,273 --> 01:05:46,108
is that every time I close my eyes,

1183
01:05:47,860 --> 01:05:49,654
it's not you that I see.

1184
01:05:51,614 --> 01:05:53,449
Who do you see?

1185
01:06:22,103 --> 01:06:23,896
<i>Prepared breakfast for you.</i>

1186
01:06:23,980 --> 01:06:26,983
<i>I went ahead. I still have a makeup class.</i>

1187
01:06:38,077 --> 01:06:39,161
Oh damn!

1188
01:06:40,496 --> 01:06:41,330
Oh!

1189
01:06:42,790 --> 01:06:43,958
I thought you left.

1190
01:06:44,875 --> 01:06:46,669
Couldn't I have just taken a shower first?

1191
01:06:48,421 --> 01:06:49,672
Don't you have water at your place?

1192
01:06:50,297 --> 01:06:52,466
You should eat. Go eat.

1193
01:06:52,550 --> 01:06:54,176
Eat already!

1194
01:06:55,720 --> 01:06:58,389
I prepared that. I know you're hungry.

1195
01:07:12,069 --> 01:07:13,487
Aren't you going to eat?

1196
01:07:14,238 --> 01:07:15,322
Later.

1197
01:07:16,073 --> 01:07:18,451
Fine, don't. You're so fussy.

1198
01:08:06,624 --> 01:08:07,708
<i>Hey, RR.</i>

1199
01:08:07,792 --> 01:08:11,212
<i>I'm reminding you about your interview</i>
<i>with our head of volunteers.</i>

1200
01:08:11,295 --> 01:08:12,171
<i>Don't forget!</i>

1201
01:08:20,846 --> 01:08:24,558
Why do you care if the one I see now
is RR and not Kenzo?

1202
01:08:24,642 --> 01:08:25,518
Huh?

1203
01:08:28,062 --> 01:08:30,439
Sis, you're so out of it again!

1204
01:08:30,523 --> 01:08:33,109
Okay, are you even done
reading all of your cases

1205
01:08:33,192 --> 01:08:35,569
or writing any of your case digests?

1206
01:08:38,114 --> 01:08:39,740
This is so unlike you!

1207
01:08:39,824 --> 01:08:42,785
And you've had so many absences already!

1208
01:08:42,868 --> 01:08:44,161
What's happening?

1209
01:08:45,496 --> 01:08:46,539
Nothing.

1210
01:08:47,498 --> 01:08:50,751
Maybe I'm just a bit out of focus lately.

1211
01:08:51,293 --> 01:08:54,672
Does this have something to do
with your shadow?

1212
01:08:54,755 --> 01:08:55,798
Shadow?

1213
01:08:56,549 --> 01:08:57,591
Shadow.

1214
01:09:01,095 --> 01:09:01,971
Here it is!

1215
01:09:02,054 --> 01:09:03,389
What?

1216
01:09:03,472 --> 01:09:06,809
What? You're so dramatic!

1217
01:09:07,601 --> 01:09:08,519
What?

1218
01:09:08,602 --> 01:09:10,312
We already kissed.

1219
01:09:10,855 --> 01:09:11,856
You kissed?

1220
01:09:13,399 --> 01:09:15,359
Hey! You're so loud!

1221
01:09:15,442 --> 01:09:16,902
Whatever.

1222
01:09:16,986 --> 01:09:19,780
So did he kiss you? Did you kiss him?

1223
01:09:19,864 --> 01:09:22,324
- Does that even matter?
- Yeah, of course!

1224
01:09:22,408 --> 01:09:24,076
So are you guys official now?

1225
01:09:24,660 --> 01:09:29,832
Yeah, kind of like some situation…

1226
01:09:30,499 --> 01:09:31,834
Situationship?

1227
01:09:32,501 --> 01:09:33,419
Oh no.

1228
01:09:36,380 --> 01:09:37,840
Something happened earlier.

1229
01:09:37,923 --> 01:09:39,341
Something already happened?

1230
01:09:39,425 --> 01:09:41,969
Okay, your shadow is moving fast.

1231
01:09:42,052 --> 01:09:43,429
You're crazy!

1232
01:09:43,512 --> 01:09:44,638
I mean…

1233
01:09:45,181 --> 01:09:47,766
That annoying Sue sent a message again.

1234
01:09:48,350 --> 01:09:50,644
It looks like
they're really going to Sudan.

1235
01:09:51,645 --> 01:09:54,148
Then tell him not to go.

1236
01:09:54,231 --> 01:09:56,650
Why would I do that? That's RR's dream.

1237
01:09:56,734 --> 01:09:59,278
Yes, but how about you?

1238
01:09:59,361 --> 01:10:00,946
How about you guys?

1239
01:10:02,156 --> 01:10:03,991
Why would I make him choose?

1240
01:10:04,825 --> 01:10:06,493
Then don't make him choose.

1241
01:10:06,577 --> 01:10:08,037
The best you can do

1242
01:10:08,120 --> 01:10:10,164
is convince him

1243
01:10:11,207 --> 01:10:12,833
before anything is too late.

1244
01:10:14,084 --> 01:10:14,960
Come on!

1245
01:10:18,047 --> 01:10:18,923
Come on.

1246
01:10:19,673 --> 01:10:20,549
Come on!

1247
01:10:37,107 --> 01:10:39,693
Good thing
you didn't get caught in the rain.

1248
01:10:41,237 --> 01:10:42,112
Come back again.

1249
01:10:42,196 --> 01:10:47,034
Did RR tell you that
this place is very important to us?

1250
01:10:47,743 --> 01:10:49,995
Are you guilt-tripping me, Janine?

1251
01:10:50,955 --> 01:10:52,998
So I'll tell RR

1252
01:10:53,874 --> 01:10:55,584
not to go through with it?

1253
01:10:56,669 --> 01:10:58,337
You don't want to lose him

1254
01:10:59,713 --> 01:11:01,131
because you need him?

1255
01:11:03,926 --> 01:11:07,346
I don't want him to leave
because I know he won't be happy there.

1256
01:11:10,015 --> 01:11:13,978
He just wants to prove something.
That's why he's doing that volunteer work.

1257
01:11:15,646 --> 01:11:18,023
But I know he won't be happy there.

1258
01:11:18,649 --> 01:11:19,483
Why?

1259
01:11:22,194 --> 01:11:23,696
Because you're not there?

1260
01:11:24,321 --> 01:11:25,823
And you think

1261
01:11:26,448 --> 01:11:28,701
you're in control of his happiness?

1262
01:11:29,451 --> 01:11:31,120
Do you hear

1263
01:11:31,203 --> 01:11:33,622
how selfish you sound, Janine?

1264
01:11:33,706 --> 01:11:35,332
Yes, I'm selfish.

1265
01:11:35,416 --> 01:11:36,333
Stupid.

1266
01:11:37,376 --> 01:11:38,377
I know.

1267
01:11:39,628 --> 01:11:43,048
I'm stupid because I thought
this time would never come.

1268
01:11:44,174 --> 01:11:46,593
The possibility that he would leave.

1269
01:11:48,429 --> 01:11:50,431
I admit that was my fault.

1270
01:11:51,932 --> 01:11:53,767
But I'm not my mistake, Sue.

1271
01:11:55,519 --> 01:11:57,896
I don't want to be defined by my mistake.

1272
01:11:58,897 --> 01:12:00,107
You're wrong.

1273
01:12:01,025 --> 01:12:04,111
His happiness doesn't depend on me.

1274
01:12:04,820 --> 01:12:08,157
My happiness depends on him.

1275
01:12:11,910 --> 01:12:14,079
So I'm begging you, Sue.

1276
01:12:15,414 --> 01:12:18,125
Please don't take away my happiness.

1277
01:12:20,502 --> 01:12:21,587
Janine…

1278
01:12:26,675 --> 01:12:30,471
The final decision is his, Janine.

1279
01:12:31,221 --> 01:12:32,890
Not mine.

1280
01:12:35,934 --> 01:12:36,935
Maybe…

1281
01:12:37,811 --> 01:12:39,480
Maybe he'll change his mind.

1282
01:12:41,315 --> 01:12:42,858
Please help me, Sue.

1283
01:12:44,902 --> 01:12:46,945
Don't let me lose him.

1284
01:12:50,616 --> 01:12:52,034
He's all I have.

1285
01:13:02,836 --> 01:13:03,712
Pip?

1286
01:13:04,922 --> 01:13:07,299
Did Sue tell you anything?

1287
01:13:07,383 --> 01:13:09,301
Nothing. Why?

1288
01:13:15,974 --> 01:13:19,228
But the person who was supposed
to interview me canceled it.

1289
01:13:19,311 --> 01:13:21,980
I don't know.
They said they'll just reschedule.

1290
01:13:24,066 --> 01:13:25,776
Maybe that's your sign.

1291
01:13:27,027 --> 01:13:27,986
Huh?

1292
01:13:28,070 --> 01:13:29,279
Not to go?

1293
01:13:39,331 --> 01:13:41,458
We have an outing this weekend.

1294
01:13:42,876 --> 01:13:43,794
Huh?

1295
01:13:44,878 --> 01:13:48,173
I signed both of us up for tree planting.

1296
01:13:48,257 --> 01:13:49,800
Jess's organization.

1297
01:13:49,883 --> 01:13:50,926
You signed me up?

1298
01:13:51,009 --> 01:13:52,344
Yeah.

1299
01:13:52,428 --> 01:13:54,471
Outsiders are allowed here, right?

1300
01:13:54,555 --> 01:13:55,722
You can invite Otep.

1301
01:13:55,806 --> 01:13:57,766
Who knows?
They might become a couple there.

1302
01:14:03,856 --> 01:14:06,358
So dirty here and I'm so tired.

1303
01:14:06,984 --> 01:14:08,235
Excuse me.

1304
01:14:09,027 --> 01:14:10,320
- I'll help you.
- Sorry.

1305
01:14:10,404 --> 01:14:13,240
I don't want your help.
We're not even close.

1306
01:14:13,323 --> 01:14:14,450
Wow.

1307
01:14:14,533 --> 01:14:15,951
Nice to meet you.

1308
01:14:16,660 --> 01:14:19,496
Are you a future law school?

1309
01:14:19,580 --> 01:14:20,456
Student.

1310
01:14:20,539 --> 01:14:21,999
Future law student.

1311
01:14:22,791 --> 01:14:24,042
Wow!

1312
01:14:24,126 --> 01:14:26,128
Oh wow!

1313
01:14:26,211 --> 01:14:28,213
Smooth! There's a spark!

1314
01:14:30,966 --> 01:14:32,384
Another one! There's a spark!

1315
01:14:32,468 --> 01:14:34,052
- There's…
- Really? Like that?

1316
01:14:35,512 --> 01:14:36,388
There it is!

1317
01:14:36,472 --> 01:14:37,806
So sweet!

1318
01:14:41,226 --> 01:14:43,437
Oh my!

1319
01:14:43,520 --> 01:14:45,105
That's a spark!

1320
01:14:47,107 --> 01:14:48,400
There's a spark!

1321
01:14:48,484 --> 01:14:50,986
- Right?
- Let's go!

1322
01:14:51,069 --> 01:14:52,654
Two already.

1323
01:14:52,738 --> 01:14:54,656
- Really?
- Yes.

1324
01:14:54,740 --> 01:14:56,366
Don't get so close to me.

1325
01:14:58,660 --> 01:14:59,536
Oh my god.

1326
01:15:02,122 --> 01:15:03,624
Oh, I didn't mean to.

1327
01:15:03,707 --> 01:15:05,125
I didn't mean to.

1328
01:15:05,209 --> 01:15:07,711
The soil was so hard. It went like that.

1329
01:15:10,130 --> 01:15:11,882
Oh really?

1330
01:15:13,258 --> 01:15:14,468
Really?

1331
01:15:14,551 --> 01:15:16,345
- I swear I didn't mean it!
- Hey!

1332
01:15:16,428 --> 01:15:17,513
You did it on purpose!

1333
01:15:17,596 --> 01:15:19,014
- Hey!
- Sorry.

1334
01:15:19,097 --> 01:15:21,058
It was hard! It just moved like that!

1335
01:15:24,520 --> 01:15:25,812
Like that!

1336
01:15:27,523 --> 01:15:28,941
You're so gross!

1337
01:15:29,024 --> 01:15:29,983
Bro, you covered me with soil!

1338
01:15:30,067 --> 01:15:32,402
- Yeah!
- Now we're both dirty!

1339
01:15:33,820 --> 01:15:35,989
- I didn't mean to make you dirty!
- There!

1340
01:15:42,704 --> 01:15:43,622
Right!

1341
01:15:45,457 --> 01:15:47,209
Hey, I just ate!

1342
01:15:47,292 --> 01:15:48,418
Ew!

1343
01:15:50,379 --> 01:15:51,922
Wait a minute! Not my face!

1344
01:15:52,005 --> 01:15:53,924
- Stop! Stop it!
- I'm sorry!

1345
01:15:54,007 --> 01:15:56,343
- You're so fussy!
- Why did I eat it?

1346
01:15:56,426 --> 01:15:58,887
- We've leveled up!
- I'm just explaining.

1347
01:15:58,971 --> 01:16:02,516
Before, we used to debrief on the rooftop.

1348
01:16:03,141 --> 01:16:04,560
Thanks, Bulots.

1349
01:16:07,187 --> 01:16:08,480
I realized a lot.

1350
01:16:09,314 --> 01:16:11,066
Especially about our passion.

1351
01:16:11,733 --> 01:16:13,360
What did you realize?

1352
01:16:14,945 --> 01:16:15,946
When…

1353
01:16:16,947 --> 01:16:19,783
When you realized you wanted
to take up environmental law,

1354
01:16:21,702 --> 01:16:23,912
I figured out what I wanted in my life.

1355
01:16:24,871 --> 01:16:26,832
What I should focus on in life.

1356
01:16:27,916 --> 01:16:28,750
This.

1357
01:16:29,459 --> 01:16:30,335
Helping.

1358
01:16:31,837 --> 01:16:32,879
Volunteering.

1359
01:16:34,590 --> 01:16:37,509
I didn't immediately figure out
what I wanted.

1360
01:16:39,344 --> 01:16:40,804
But now I do.

1361
01:16:43,265 --> 01:16:44,891
I won't give this up.

1362
01:16:46,768 --> 01:16:48,270
You're lucky.

1363
01:16:49,313 --> 01:16:50,606
Because before,

1364
01:16:51,231 --> 01:16:53,275
I almost gave up on what I wanted.

1365
01:16:54,901 --> 01:16:56,570
Even this opportunity…

1366
01:16:58,238 --> 01:16:59,698
I don't want to let it go.

1367
01:17:02,075 --> 01:17:05,996
Just because you won't go abroad

1368
01:17:06,580 --> 01:17:07,831
doesn't mean you're giving up.

1369
01:17:11,835 --> 01:17:13,462
Why don't you just stay, Pip?

1370
01:17:17,007 --> 01:17:18,967
A lot of people need you here.

1371
01:17:32,356 --> 01:17:34,566
For goodness sake, Ms. Mesina.

1372
01:17:34,650 --> 01:17:35,567
AI?

1373
01:17:35,651 --> 01:17:38,612
I thought you were
an environmental advocate?

1374
01:17:38,695 --> 01:17:43,950
Why did you use AI
to write your case digest?

1375
01:17:46,078 --> 01:17:47,746
You're a hypocrite.

1376
01:17:48,622 --> 01:17:51,249
And you think I wouldn't detect it? Huh?

1377
01:17:52,793 --> 01:17:55,003
This is so embarrassing for you.

1378
01:17:57,506 --> 01:17:59,174
Forget about your DL dreams.

1379
01:17:59,257 --> 01:18:02,886
Because most likely,
I'll give you a three.

1380
01:18:02,969 --> 01:18:05,722
Way below the cutoff.

1381
01:18:17,359 --> 01:18:19,986
- Have you tried this?
- Let's try it.

1382
01:18:20,070 --> 01:18:21,196
- Let's go here!
- Where?

1383
01:18:21,279 --> 01:18:24,449
- Did you have your breakfast?
- So delicious.

1384
01:18:24,533 --> 01:18:26,243
- I always come here.
- Try this.

1385
01:18:26,326 --> 01:18:28,912
- Sausage? Sweetened pork?
- I'll have sweetened pork.

1386
01:18:29,621 --> 01:18:31,123
Hey, RR!

1387
01:18:31,206 --> 01:18:32,999
Your best friend left this.

1388
01:18:33,083 --> 01:18:34,918
Give it to her, okay?

1389
01:18:35,001 --> 01:18:36,044
She was here?

1390
01:18:36,128 --> 01:18:38,171
Yes. She was with Sue.

1391
01:18:40,048 --> 01:18:41,883
Their steamed pork bun is also good.

1392
01:18:41,967 --> 01:18:43,427
- You want?
- The macaroni soup.

1393
01:18:43,510 --> 01:18:45,011
Okay. Okay, miss…

1394
01:18:45,095 --> 01:18:46,596
Pares mix, please.

1395
01:19:02,028 --> 01:19:03,363
<i>Where are you, Pip?</i>

1396
01:19:03,447 --> 01:19:04,740
<i>Come see me, please?</i>

1397
01:19:09,035 --> 01:19:13,081
<i>For once, can you come</i>
<i>to me instead, Janine?</i>

1398
01:19:35,729 --> 01:19:36,605
Pip?

1399
01:19:37,898 --> 01:19:39,399
- Pip, I--
- Sorry, Janine.

1400
01:19:41,985 --> 01:19:44,571
What's the problem again? Huh?

1401
01:19:45,614 --> 01:19:46,865
I don't have a problem.

1402
01:19:46,948 --> 01:19:48,074
But I do.

1403
01:19:49,493 --> 01:19:52,120
I have a problem with what you did.

1404
01:19:55,499 --> 01:19:57,584
Did you really have
to sabotage my application?

1405
01:20:01,671 --> 01:20:02,964
For what?

1406
01:20:03,590 --> 01:20:05,300
So I wouldn't leave?

1407
01:20:05,926 --> 01:20:07,135
I'm sorry, Pip.

1408
01:20:08,220 --> 01:20:11,765
I didn't mean
to sabotage your application.

1409
01:20:12,390 --> 01:20:15,060
Then what was that? What do you call that?

1410
01:20:15,894 --> 01:20:16,895
Just for fun?

1411
01:20:19,439 --> 01:20:21,691
Just say you don't want me to leave
because you're afraid

1412
01:20:21,775 --> 01:20:23,527
of being left behind.

1413
01:20:24,236 --> 01:20:25,237
Yes!

1414
01:20:27,572 --> 01:20:28,990
I'm afraid of being left behind.

1415
01:20:30,325 --> 01:20:31,243
Sorry!

1416
01:20:32,994 --> 01:20:35,163
Instead of apologizing,
maybe you should change, right?

1417
01:20:37,332 --> 01:20:39,376
You should have just talked to me directly

1418
01:20:40,585 --> 01:20:42,504
instead of doing something behind my back.

1419
01:20:44,589 --> 01:20:47,843
After everything we've been through,
you should at least give me that.

1420
01:20:51,596 --> 01:20:52,472
Pip.

1421
01:20:53,265 --> 01:20:55,225
I've told you many times, right?

1422
01:20:57,227 --> 01:21:00,272
Maybe you can just stay.

1423
01:21:00,355 --> 01:21:03,149
And how many times have I told you

1424
01:21:04,150 --> 01:21:06,528
that it really matters to me?

1425
01:21:07,779 --> 01:21:09,406
For my future.

1426
01:21:10,407 --> 01:21:11,700
You don't understand that?

1427
01:21:11,783 --> 01:21:14,494
Is it so hard to understand
that I want us to stay together?

1428
01:21:14,578 --> 01:21:17,539
Fine, for you. Right? It's always you.

1429
01:21:19,040 --> 01:21:21,042
It's always you. Always Ja…

1430
01:21:21,126 --> 01:21:22,836
Always Janine!

1431
01:21:26,464 --> 01:21:28,383
Why is it always you, huh?

1432
01:21:31,553 --> 01:21:33,513
When you're sick, who's with you?

1433
01:21:33,597 --> 01:21:35,390
When you have a problem,

1434
01:21:36,224 --> 01:21:37,517
who solves it for you?

1435
01:21:39,686 --> 01:21:42,522
When you have enemies,
who's on your side? Isn't it me?

1436
01:21:44,441 --> 01:21:45,817
That's my fault, Pip.

1437
01:21:48,361 --> 01:21:49,279
I'm sorry.

1438
01:21:50,322 --> 01:21:52,824
Right, Pip? You said I should change
instead of apologizing.

1439
01:21:52,908 --> 01:21:55,785
I will. Here it is. I'll change!

1440
01:21:55,869 --> 01:21:58,246
Pip… Pip, I'll change.

1441
01:21:58,330 --> 01:22:00,248
Please don't leave me, Pip.

1442
01:22:00,790 --> 01:22:02,542
I'll do anything for you, Pip.

1443
01:22:03,919 --> 01:22:05,170
- Janine.
- Pip.

1444
01:22:11,259 --> 01:22:13,011
I wish I'd realized this sooner.

1445
01:22:13,094 --> 01:22:14,179
Yeah.

1446
01:22:14,846 --> 01:22:16,473
You really should have.

1447
01:22:17,849 --> 01:22:20,977
Because damn it! I've loved you all along!

1448
01:22:25,273 --> 01:22:27,025
I'm mad at myself

1449
01:22:28,109 --> 01:22:30,070
because I want to be mad at you,

1450
01:22:31,738 --> 01:22:33,156
but I can't.

1451
01:22:35,909 --> 01:22:38,161
Because I know I'll keep coming back.

1452
01:22:42,123 --> 01:22:45,210
Whether you like it or not,
my whole life revolves around you.

1453
01:22:49,923 --> 01:22:51,841
So please let me walk away now.

1454
01:22:52,634 --> 01:22:54,386
No….

1455
01:22:54,469 --> 01:22:56,554
- I need to walk away from you now.
- Pip…

1456
01:22:57,305 --> 01:22:59,307
Pip, sorry. Please.

1457
01:23:00,642 --> 01:23:02,227
I'll do anything, Pip.

1458
01:23:02,310 --> 01:23:04,479
Pip. Pip, I'll do anything.

1459
01:23:04,562 --> 01:23:07,190
Please don't leave me.

1460
01:23:07,273 --> 01:23:10,735
Pip… This isn't supposed
to be our ending, right?

1461
01:23:11,403 --> 01:23:13,822
Please don't leave me, Pip.

1462
01:23:13,905 --> 01:23:15,115
Pip.

1463
01:23:18,868 --> 01:23:20,078
Janine.

1464
01:23:23,123 --> 01:23:25,041
I'm not a character in your stories.

1465
01:23:29,254 --> 01:23:30,839
This is real life.

1466
01:23:35,093 --> 01:23:37,637
In all your stories,
you're always the main character.

1467
01:23:40,640 --> 01:23:41,891
Can it be me this time?

1468
01:23:47,689 --> 01:23:49,065
I'm sorry.

1469
01:23:49,899 --> 01:23:51,693
I'm sorry…

1470
01:23:52,402 --> 01:23:53,361
Pip.

1471
01:24:42,285 --> 01:24:45,789
<i>Mom, I'll come home this weekend.</i>

1472
01:25:00,845 --> 01:25:01,721
Ma.

1473
01:25:11,523 --> 01:25:13,358
It's okay.

1474
01:25:17,904 --> 01:25:19,322
It's okay.

1475
01:25:19,405 --> 01:25:20,907
Ma, I failed.

1476
01:25:22,867 --> 01:25:25,328
Want to sit down? Let's sit.

1477
01:25:28,790 --> 01:25:29,999
I failed school.

1478
01:25:31,709 --> 01:25:33,128
I failed RR.

1479
01:25:34,754 --> 01:25:36,464
And I failed you.

1480
01:25:42,887 --> 01:25:44,180
I'm sorry.

1481
01:25:45,056 --> 01:25:46,391
I'm sorry.

1482
01:25:48,560 --> 01:25:50,186
I'm sorry, Ma.

1483
01:25:52,897 --> 01:25:54,649
I'm sorry.

1484
01:26:03,992 --> 01:26:07,871
Do you know how many times

1485
01:26:08,997 --> 01:26:11,249
I almost failed in law school?

1486
01:26:18,506 --> 01:26:19,799
Did you think

1487
01:26:20,633 --> 01:26:22,677
I didn't struggle with the bar exam?

1488
01:26:24,721 --> 01:26:26,514
Have you thought of

1489
01:26:26,598 --> 01:26:30,852
how many times I loved

1490
01:26:32,478 --> 01:26:36,441
and got hurt before I met your dad?

1491
01:26:37,567 --> 01:26:41,946
And how many times we almost

1492
01:26:42,030 --> 01:26:44,699
gave up on each other.

1493
01:26:46,367 --> 01:26:48,077
How did you endure that, Ma?

1494
01:26:49,579 --> 01:26:50,413
I mean…

1495
01:26:51,080 --> 01:26:53,458
How do I become like you?

1496
01:26:55,168 --> 01:26:58,630
An Attorney Mesina.

1497
01:27:00,256 --> 01:27:01,382
My child,

1498
01:27:02,258 --> 01:27:04,135
I became who I am

1499
01:27:04,219 --> 01:27:06,471
not because I always win

1500
01:27:07,597 --> 01:27:09,307
or I'm always right.

1501
01:27:10,433 --> 01:27:12,602
I am who I am

1502
01:27:13,436 --> 01:27:15,772
because I can move on

1503
01:27:16,940 --> 01:27:18,274
when I make mistakes.

1504
01:27:20,652 --> 01:27:21,736
And besides,

1505
01:27:22,278 --> 01:27:25,907
there's already
an Attorney Marissa Mesina.

1506
01:27:28,076 --> 01:27:30,411
You just be Janine Mesina.

1507
01:27:37,418 --> 01:27:39,337
Everything is going to be okay.

1508
01:27:42,382 --> 01:27:44,425
I'm so proud of you.

1509
01:29:00,918 --> 01:29:02,211
<i>Dear Sir/Madam,</i>

1510
01:29:03,671 --> 01:29:08,009
<i>I strongly recommend</i>
<i>Mr. Raymond Richard Velasco,</i>

1511
01:29:09,093 --> 01:29:10,345
<i>RR.</i>

1512
01:29:11,554 --> 01:29:15,099
<i>I can confidently say</i>
<i>that he possesses the hard work,</i>

1513
01:29:15,683 --> 01:29:17,643
<i>determination,</i>

1514
01:29:18,353 --> 01:29:21,314
<i>and compassion required</i>
<i>for humanitarian work.</i>

1515
01:29:22,815 --> 01:29:25,318
<i>To most, he is RR.</i>

1516
01:29:27,612 --> 01:29:28,821
<i>But to me,</i>

1517
01:29:29,614 --> 01:29:30,823
<i>he is Pip.</i>

1518
01:29:31,574 --> 01:29:34,202
<i>I have known him since we were children.</i>

1519
01:29:36,162 --> 01:29:37,663
<i>He is selfless,</i>

1520
01:29:38,706 --> 01:29:40,666
<i>always putting others before himself.</i>

1521
01:29:42,710 --> 01:29:47,048
<i>He would give up what is his</i>
<i>just to help others.</i>

1522
01:29:47,632 --> 01:29:51,761
<i>That's the kind of volunteer</i>
<i>that would excel in your organization.</i>

1523
01:29:53,179 --> 01:29:54,889
<i>I will miss my Pip.</i>

1524
01:29:57,600 --> 01:29:59,685
<i>But the world deserves him too.</i>

1525
01:30:01,187 --> 01:30:02,814
<i>His generosity,</i>

1526
01:30:02,897 --> 01:30:04,232
<i>his service,</i>

1527
01:30:04,315 --> 01:30:05,775
<i>and his humanity.</i>

1528
01:30:35,638 --> 01:30:36,806
You?

1529
01:30:45,898 --> 01:30:46,774
Bulots?

1530
01:30:59,370 --> 01:31:01,330
I know what you're going to say.

1531
01:31:02,915 --> 01:31:04,876
As long as I'm here,

1532
01:31:05,543 --> 01:31:07,211
they will not stop.

1533
01:31:09,297 --> 01:31:11,090
I need to stay away…

1534
01:31:13,426 --> 01:31:14,635
for you…

1535
01:31:17,263 --> 01:31:18,264
and for me.

1536
01:31:19,432 --> 01:31:21,267
I understand.

1537
01:31:22,059 --> 01:31:23,686
I understand.

1538
01:31:24,770 --> 01:31:27,148
There are also a lot of people
who need you.

1539
01:31:28,774 --> 01:31:30,318
Not just me.

1540
01:31:34,864 --> 01:31:36,324
So you're ready to let me go?

1541
01:31:37,408 --> 01:31:38,868
Not yet…

1542
01:31:42,455 --> 01:31:45,124
because you're forgetting something.

1543
01:32:29,335 --> 01:32:31,254
<i>Janine, where are you?</i>

1544
01:32:32,129 --> 01:32:33,506
<i>Won't you even say goodbye?</i>

1545
01:32:33,589 --> 01:32:35,383
<i>A send-off?</i>

1546
01:32:35,466 --> 01:32:37,134
A send-off?

1547
01:32:37,218 --> 01:32:38,552
For whom?

1548
01:32:42,098 --> 01:32:43,474
For RR.

1549
01:32:44,100 --> 01:32:46,477
<i>He's already been called in for training.</i>

1550
01:32:47,478 --> 01:32:50,940
It seems things are going well.
There's an opening for trainees.

1551
01:32:51,524 --> 01:32:53,401
He's highly recommended by someone.

1552
01:32:54,610 --> 01:32:55,653
Really?

1553
01:32:58,197 --> 01:32:59,782
Wait.

1554
01:32:59,865 --> 01:33:00,866
When is he leaving?

1555
01:33:00,950 --> 01:33:02,702
Tonight.

1556
01:33:02,785 --> 01:33:03,828
What?

1557
01:33:13,379 --> 01:33:15,047
Miss, this is a holdup.

1558
01:33:15,673 --> 01:33:16,674
Give me your things.

1559
01:33:16,757 --> 01:33:20,344
My boyfriend's flight is today.

1560
01:33:20,428 --> 01:33:23,472
What are you talking about?
Are you crazy? Give me your things.

1561
01:33:25,391 --> 01:33:27,101
Your cellphone too.

1562
01:33:27,184 --> 01:33:28,019
Give it to me.

1563
01:33:30,521 --> 01:33:31,689
Driver, stop the vehicle!

1564
01:34:05,973 --> 01:34:07,641
How selfish!

1565
01:34:17,735 --> 01:34:19,779
I'm sorry, okay?

1566
01:34:19,862 --> 01:34:21,280
I'm sorry.

1567
01:34:23,741 --> 01:34:26,827
I'm sorry if I was being too selfish.

1568
01:34:28,120 --> 01:34:30,790
I'm sorry if I got scared.

1569
01:34:37,254 --> 01:34:40,925
But you could have at least
let me say goodbye to you.

1570
01:34:43,386 --> 01:34:47,723
Pip, I love you so much!

1571
01:34:50,142 --> 01:34:52,228
I love you so much, Pip.

1572
01:35:14,166 --> 01:35:16,544
Can you please repeat what you said?

1573
01:35:18,254 --> 01:35:20,214
I didn't hear everything that you said.

1574
01:35:21,882 --> 01:35:23,884
From the top, please.

1575
01:35:28,180 --> 01:35:32,268
Also, why do you writers
think rain is romantic?

1576
01:35:32,351 --> 01:35:35,187
Even though you'll just end up
with a cold or fever after that.

1577
01:35:35,271 --> 01:35:37,064
Pip!

1578
01:35:41,986 --> 01:35:42,945
Here's your umbrella.

1579
01:35:44,613 --> 01:35:47,741
You left it at the eatery the other day.

1580
01:35:52,413 --> 01:35:53,372
Pip.

1581
01:35:55,374 --> 01:35:58,377
It's okay if you want to leave.

1582
01:36:02,131 --> 01:36:04,216
You don't have to stay just for me.

1583
01:36:06,760 --> 01:36:10,431
After all the trouble you caused,
you're just going to make me leave anyway?

1584
01:36:12,141 --> 01:36:13,309
No.

1585
01:36:15,227 --> 01:36:16,103
Bulots…

1586
01:36:17,480 --> 01:36:19,940
When did I leave
without saying goodbye to you?

1587
01:36:22,526 --> 01:36:23,819
I'm serious.

1588
01:36:24,862 --> 01:36:26,280
It's real life now.

1589
01:36:28,616 --> 01:36:30,743
Whatever makes you happy.

1590
01:36:30,826 --> 01:36:32,369
It's only for a moment anyway.

1591
01:36:33,996 --> 01:36:35,581
We can do it, right?

1592
01:36:39,376 --> 01:36:41,921
After all the time we've been together,

1593
01:36:42,004 --> 01:36:43,422
just like I told you,

1594
01:36:45,382 --> 01:36:47,468
I'll always come back to you.

1595
01:36:52,681 --> 01:36:54,099
You're really annoying.

1596
01:36:55,059 --> 01:36:57,228
You look so handsome when you smile.

1597
01:37:03,859 --> 01:37:04,735
Hey!

1598
01:37:05,736 --> 01:37:09,156
Aren't you going to compliment me too?
Am I ugly?

1599
01:37:09,240 --> 01:37:13,536
I already said you're handsome.
I'm waiting for you to say I'm beautiful.

1600
01:37:13,619 --> 01:37:17,873
You don't find me beautiful anymore
ever since you met that girl?

1601
01:37:17,957 --> 01:37:21,210
Why are you smiling? You're leaving and…

1602
01:38:38,078 --> 01:38:39,038
Take one.

1603
01:38:49,256 --> 01:38:50,424
Sorry.

1604
01:38:51,133 --> 01:38:52,009
Sorry.

1605
01:38:53,886 --> 01:38:55,012
Wait.

1606
01:38:59,350 --> 01:39:01,435
Your delivery was bad.

1607
01:39:02,603 --> 01:39:04,104
You might wake up.

1608
01:39:05,272 --> 01:39:06,398
Try it.

1609
01:39:11,779 --> 01:39:13,822
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1610
01:39:16,825 --> 01:39:17,785
Hey!

1611
01:39:18,786 --> 01:39:20,579
- Try it.
- Answer.

1612
01:39:21,872 --> 01:39:24,416
- Cut!
- Damn it. Why is it like that?

1613
01:39:25,459 --> 01:39:27,252
Look at your chest.

1614
01:39:27,336 --> 01:39:29,421
There. Position your chest.
Adjust your chest.

1615
01:39:29,505 --> 01:39:32,341
Okay, go on. Do it. Show me.

1616
01:39:32,424 --> 01:39:34,510
